    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a33a815_fcda2cad",
        "filename": "aom/aom_image.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T23:45:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please see my comment at av1/decoder/obu.c:1064. It is better to document that `aom_metadata_t::insert_flag` is not used by the decoder, and the placeholder value set by the decoder should be ignored.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 168,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 171,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "9182de0a11cf28074759cc6bf6c34971916d56ab",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "661a4b3f_83e2b5ba",
        "filename": "aom/aom_image.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 26789
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-24T14:41:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that users of the decoder API might need to know if a metadata OBU is layer specific or not, in cases where both are allowed. This way they will know which layers to apply the metadata to (all of them, or only the current layer).",
      "parentUuid": "3a33a815_fcda2cad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 168,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 171,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "9182de0a11cf28074759cc6bf6c34971916d56ab",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f497a52a_ab7dd7cf",
        "filename": "aom/aom_image.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-24T23:40:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... You are right. Although the `aom_image_t` struct has the `temporal_id` and `spatial_id` fields, when they are both 0 it is ambiguous whether they are explicitly set to 0 in the OBU extension header or they are assigned the default value 0 because the OBU extension header is absent. So it is useful to report whether the OBU extension header is present. Note that this is not exactly the same as whether the OBU is layer-specific, but it is a good approximation. The two booleans differ only when there is only one layer, in which case it doesn\u0027t really matter whether an OBU is layer-specific.",
      "parentUuid": "661a4b3f_83e2b5ba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 168,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 171,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "9182de0a11cf28074759cc6bf6c34971916d56ab",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
