      "key": {
        "uuid": "86e6d57d_a57d9b0b",
        "filename": "av1/decoder/obu.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1064,
      "author": {
        "id": 26789
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-24T14:41:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right that there is a subtle semantics difference, but in practice I don\u0027t think it really matters. If there is only one layer, it it\u0027s the same thing if an OBU applies to all layers or only to the current layer. In practice, this boolean determines whether we output the OBU with AOM_MIF_ANY_FRAME or AOM_MIF_ANY_FRAME_LAYER_SPECIFIC. In aom_image.h, I did write that the latter is used only \"when the video contains multiple layers\".\n\nNote that the spec doesn\u0027t actually describe what should be done for OBUs that can optionally be layer-specific, except for the Padding OBU: \"Padding OBUs may or may not be layer-specific. If the obu_extension_flag is set to 1 they are layer-specific, whereas when the obu_extension_flag is set to 0 they are not.\"",
      "parentUuid": "9ce57263_75bdf482",
      "revId": "9182de0a11cf28074759cc6bf6c34971916d56ab",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
